WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.974 --> 00:00:20.467
"I wish I were invisible," said Jimmy.

2
00:00:21.368 --> 00:00:24.090
The children were walking along in the growing darkness.

3
00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:26.092
"I'd be a burglar."

4
00:00:26.112 --> 00:00:28.614
"It's wrong to steal!"

5
00:00:28.954 --> 00:00:30.816
cried Kathleen and Mabel together.

6
00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.321
"Then I'd be a detective," said Jimmy.

7
00:00:35.341 --> 00:00:40.584
"That's what I'll do," said Gerald, who really was invisible.

8
00:00:41.664 --> 00:00:44.425
"Let's go to the police station and see if they need help."

9
00:00:45.506 --> 00:00:47.847
Outside the police station was a notice board.

10
00:00:50.308 --> 00:00:51.708
Two dogs had been lost.

11
00:00:52.749 --> 00:00:53.649
So had a purse.

12
00:00:54.569 --> 00:00:56.530
Gerald wasn't interested in any of that.

13
00:00:57.871 --> 00:01:01.012
Another notice announced that a mansion had been burglarized.

14
00:01:02.064 --> 00:01:05.005
Some silver candlesticks and serving dishes were stolen.

15
00:01:05.025 --> 00:01:07.646
"I'll catch those burglars!"

16
00:01:08.187 --> 00:01:09.087
Gerald decided.

17
00:01:09.107 --> 00:01:11.768
"There's Officer Johnson.

18
00:01:12.208 --> 00:01:14.069
Go ask him what he knows about the crime."

19
00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:19.871
The visible children talked to the policeman, but he didn't have much to say.

20
00:01:19.891 --> 00:01:23.873
"Officer Johnson thinks he knows who did it.

21
00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:27.454
But he needs proof," Jimmy reported back to Gerald.

22
00:01:27.474 --> 00:01:31.276
"You're not much help," Gerald replied.

23
00:01:33.024 --> 00:01:36.126
"You didn't even find out how or when the silver was taken.

24
00:01:36.607 --> 00:01:37.767
Go home and eat your supper."

25
00:01:39.409 --> 00:01:40.930
"What will you do about supper?"

26
00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.812
Mabel asked Gerald as they started walking again.

27
00:01:43.832 --> 00:01:47.474
"I'm hoping one of you will buy me some buns."

28
00:01:51.397 --> 00:01:55.660
The children stopped outside the bakery, and Kathleen and Jimmy went inside.

29
00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:59.002
"Oh!" Mabel suddenly cried.

30
00:01:59.022 --> 00:02:00.643
"What's wrong?"

31
00:02:01.123 --> 00:02:01.724
asked Gerald.

32
00:02:02.676 --> 00:02:06.218
"I just remembered I left the window open in the treasure room.

33
00:02:07.899 --> 00:02:09.340
I have to go back right now.

34
00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.161
My aunt will be so angry!

35
00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:13.982
The treasure room door is locked from the inside.

36
00:02:14.483 --> 00:02:18.065
She'll have to ask the gardener to get a ladder and climb through the window."

37
00:02:18.085 --> 00:02:20.886
"Don't worry," Gerald said.

38
00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:23.048
"I can climb through the window."

39
00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:30.712
They turned around while Jimmy and Kathleen continued home for supper.

40
00:02:37.192 --> 00:02:38.253
"Late again!"

41
00:02:38.793 --> 00:02:41.274
exclaimed Mademoiselle when the two of them arrived.

42
00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:44.075
"And where is Gerald?"

43
00:02:44.095 --> 00:02:49.337
"Uh he has a headache," said Jimmy.

44
00:02:49.357 --> 00:02:51.538
"He went straight to bed."

45
00:02:51.558 --> 00:02:53.639
"Poor boy.

46
00:02:54.159 --> 00:02:56.880
I'll bring him some supper," said Mademoiselle.

47
00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:01.202
"No, no," said Kathleen quickly.

48
00:03:01.222 --> 00:03:04.463
"He never eats when he has a headache."

49
00:03:05.524 --> 00:03:07.597
"Oh well," said Mademoiselle.

50
00:03:07.617 --> 00:03:09.958
"Hurry up and eat your supper."

51
00:03:10.898 --> 00:03:12.939
And she went back to reading some old letters.

52
00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.481
Meanwhile Gerald and Mabel arrived at the castle.

53
00:03:17.882 --> 00:03:20.083
Mabel knocked on the door the servants used.

54
00:03:22.465 --> 00:03:23.505
"Oh Mabel!"

55
00:03:23.945 --> 00:03:25.626
cried her aunt as she opened the door.

56
00:03:25.646 --> 00:03:28.428
"Thank goodness you're safe!"

57
00:03:29.348 --> 00:03:31.109
She gave Mabel a big hug.

58
00:03:31.129 --> 00:03:36.152
"I don't know what was wrong with me," said the aunt.

59
00:03:37.204 --> 00:03:39.585
"Yesterday I didn't care anything about you.

60
00:03:41.305 --> 00:03:45.186
The same thing happened when I got your note and when some children visited.

61
00:03:45.906 --> 00:03:50.768
But this afternoon I suddenly awoke from my trance and realized you were gone.

62
00:03:51.588 --> 00:03:52.688
It was awful!"

63
00:03:53.769 --> 00:03:56.469
Mabel's aunt pulled her into the castle and shut the door.

64
00:03:56.489 --> 00:04:02.711
"That was very strange," said Gerald, who was left outside in the dark.

65
00:04:03.731 --> 00:04:05.452
"It seems like more magic to me."

66
00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:09.682
Gerald began looking for the open window of the treasure room.

67
00:04:10.643 --> 00:04:14.646
The castle gardens were so beautiful that he felt he was in another world.

68
00:04:14.666 --> 00:04:19.269
"Everything looks so different at night," he thought.

69
00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:23.272
Something white moved under a willow tree.

70
00:04:25.513 --> 00:04:29.676
The creature had a goat's horns and legs, but the head and arms of a boy.

71
00:04:30.577 --> 00:04:34.740
It stretched its legs, rolled on the grass, and then ran across the lawn.

72
00:04:35.692 --> 00:04:38.694
The most amazing thing was that Gerald was not afraid.

73
00:04:40.095 --> 00:04:42.237
There was still something white under the tree.

74
00:04:43.278 --> 00:04:46.640
Gerald moved closer and saw a pedestal for a statue.

75
00:04:47.521 --> 00:04:48.601
But nothing stood on it.

76
00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:51.483
"The statues he murmured.

77
00:04:52.804 --> 00:04:57.848
Just then another statue walked out of the Temple of Flora and disappeared into some bushes.

78
00:04:57.868 --> 00:05:00.010
"They come alive!"
